course: dictionary
lesson: 8002
title: Re- means again
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A prefix is a few letters added to the front of a word that change its meaning. The prefix re- means again. So to redo something is to do it again. «Archie had to redo the work» means he had to do the work a second time.
explain: Check the word in two parts: re + do. Do means to carry out an action, so redo means to carry it out once more. The same pattern works with other words: rewrite is to write again, and replay is to play again.
explain: Redo can be a verb or a noun. As a verb it is something you do: «redo the sum», «redo your working». In informal talk, a redo is a second try, a do-over, as when a child asks for a redo in a game. Redo can also mean to decorate a room again, as in «having the kitchen redone».
fact: A prefix is a few letters added to the front of a word that change its meaning.
fact: Re- means again, so redo means do again.
fact: «Redo» can mean to decorate a room again, and this does not always mean something went wrong.
fact: The forms are redo, redoes, redid and redone: «She redid the sum», «The kitchen has been redone».
fact: Other prefixes work the same way: mis- means wrongly (misread), pre- means before (preview), and dis- means not (disagree).
exercise: «Archie had to redo the work.» What does redo mean here? | *To do it again | To hand it in early | To throw the work away | To copy it from a friend
exercise: What does the prefix re- mean in rewrite? | Before | Not | *Again | Wrongly
exercise: «Having the kitchen redone means builders take the old one out and put a new one in.» What happens to the kitchen when it is redone? | It gets smaller | It is sold to another family | *The old kitchen is taken out and a new one is put in | The walls are painted and nothing else changes
test: In informal talk, what is a redo? | *A second try, a do-over | A kind of cake | A mistake that cannot be fixed | A bad mark from the teacher
test: Which word has re- meaning again? | Disagree | Submarine | *Replay | Preview
exam: Ayesha says redo means do before. Why is she wrong? | Re- means wrongly, so redo means do badly | Re- means under, so redo means do underneath | Re- means not, so redo means do nothing | *Re- means again, so redo means do again
